message: >-
  If you use this study or its audit methodology, please cite it (software
  metadata below). Citation author is the GitHub account; no institutional
  affiliation exists at this time.
title: >-
  Does Fisher-Rao geometry between candidate futures add information to
  token-level uncertainty monitors? A pre-registered falsification on
  Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct / GSM8K
authors:
  - alias: piplupjuice
type: dataset
version: v1.2
date-released: 2026-10-17
url: https://github.com/piplupjuice/fisher-rao-llm-monitor
repository-code: https://github.com/piplupjuice/fisher-rao-llm-monitor
license: MIT
keywords:
  - information geometry
  - Fisher-Rao
  - uncertainty estimation
  - LLM monitoring
  - negative result
  - pre-registration
  - falsification
  - GSM8K
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A controlled, pre-registered test of whether Fisher-Rao distances between
  candidate future continuations add incremental predictive information to
  conventional token-level uncertainty features (entropy, NLL, length) for
  monitor-classified answer correctness. Target model: Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct,
  dataset: GSM8K, 500 questions, frozen split, deterministic decoding.
  Result: null for incremental Fisher-Rao information under the tested
  regime; an earlier confounded 0.84 AUROC estimate is decomposed and
  corrected in-artifact. Full audit trail included.
